{#
	How a file field is drawn: what is on the record now, a way to replace it, and
	a tick to take it off (XIV-115).

	**A form theme rather than a template around the widget**, for the reason
	`markdown.html.twig` gives one block along: nothing renders a record's fields
	one at a time: `RecordForm` calls `form_widget(form.fields)` once and knows
	nothing about what is in it, so a block keyed on this form type's own prefix
	is the only way to give one kind of field its own appearance without something
	upstream learning that it exists.

	**The hidden control is rendered first and is the value.** Everything else here
	is furniture: the file input exists so the browser has somewhere to put a file,
	and the tick exists so a file can come off. If this block ever stops drawing
	`stored`, every record with a file on it loses it on the next save. See
	Xivi\Core\Form\RecordFileType, which explains why the value travels that way.

	**No download link here, deliberately.** A form knows the shape it is drawing
	and not which record it is drawing it for, and the download route is addressed
	by module and record id (§8.4). Rather than thread two route parameters through
	the engine so that an edit form can offer what the record page already offers
	one click away, the form names the file it is holding and the record page is
	where it is opened.
#}
{% block xivi_file_widget %}
	{{- form_widget(form.stored) -}}

	{% if stored_file is not null %}
		<p class="form-text mb-1 mt-0">
			<span class="fw-medium">{{ stored_file.name }}</span>
			<span class="text-body-secondary">{{ file_size(stored_file.size) }}</span>
		</p>

		<div class="form-check mb-1">
			{{ form_widget(form.remove, {attr: {class: 'form-check-input'}}) }}
			{{ form_label(form.remove, null, {label_attr: {class: 'form-check-label'}}) }}
		</div>
	{% endif %}

	{{- form_widget(form.upload) -}}

	{# The ceiling, said where the choosing happens rather than after a refusal.
	   `max_bytes` is Xivi\Core\Field\AttachmentLimit's constant, which is also
	   what the intake measures against and what the ini files are aligned above,
	   so this sentence cannot drift away from what is actually enforced. #}
	<p class="form-text mb-0">{{ 'file.max'|trans({'%size%': file_size(max_bytes)}, 'xivi') }}</p>
{% endblock %}
